.TH HOWTO 1 "August 12, 2026" "HowTo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
howto \- turn plain English into a shell command locally
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B howto
.RI [ options ] " request ..."
.br
.B howto
.RI command
.br
.B howto setup
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B HowTo
runs a local GGUF model through llama.cpp and prints one shell command suited to
the current platform. It targets macOS with zsh and BSD tools first, and
GNU/Linux with bash. Requests do not leave the machine when using the default
provider.
.PP
Query generation requires the one-time
.B howto setup
workflow. Setup verifies the runtime, installs or reuses the model, and can
configure context-aware Tab insertion for zsh, Bash, or fish. An interactive
query offers to start missing setup. Non-interactive queries fail with an
instruction instead of prompting or consuming request input.
.PP
When the shell integration is enabled, a successful single-result command
classified as NO_KNOWN_RISK or CAUTION is available once in that shell session.
Pressing Tab at a completely empty prompt inserts it into the editable buffer
without submitting it. Tab keeps its normal completion behavior otherwise.
Pending commands become unavailable after ten minutes. Bash integration
requires Bash 4.1 or newer; the default macOS zsh is supported.
.PP
The words help and version select management commands when alone. Doctor
and setup select management parsing when alone or followed by an option. Model,
server, and config also select it when alone, or when followed by a documented
action or option. Shell requires a documented action or option.
Once selected, all remaining management arguments are validated strictly.
Use
.B --
to force query parsing for natural language with a management-shaped prefix.
.PP
Generated commands are not executed unless
.B --execute
is supplied and an interactive confirmation succeeds. Commands classified as
DANGER or UNKNOWN are never executed. The checker is a denylist and syntax
analyzer, not a sandbox; always review generated commands.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -x ", " -e ", " --execute
Execute the selected command after confirmation. Incompatible with
.B --json
and
.BR --quiet .
.TP
.BR -c ", " --copy
Copy the selected command to the clipboard.
.TP
.BR -q ", " --quiet
Print only a command with no known risk. CAUTION, DANGER, and UNKNOWN output is
refused in this mode. Incompatible with
.BR --json ,
.BR --execute ,
and a count greater than one.
.TP
.BR -n ", " --count " " N
Generate up to N alternatives, from 1 through 8.
.TP
.B --json
Emit structured JSON.
.TP
.B --timing
Print generation timing to standard error.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Show the HowTo version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup [-y|--yes] [--no-shell|--shell zsh|bash|fish]
Perform or repair required onboarding. In local mode, resolve and probe
llama-server before downloading, resuming, and verifying the pinned model.
Configured-provider mode skips the local model. By default, interactive setup
asks whether to install the Tab integration. Use
.B --yes
to accept setup prompts,
.B --no-shell
to complete setup without integration and remove prior managed hooks, or
.B --shell
to choose an integration explicitly. Open a new terminal after enabling it.
.TP
.B doctor [--json] [--deep]
Inspect setup, configuration, model, llama-server, and resident-server status.
For a configured provider, try GET /health and then GET /v1/models, using the
configured bearer token when present; this does not test chat completion. In
local mode, require a successful, 30-second llama-server --version probe.
.TP
.B model [status] [--json] [--deep]
Inspect the installed model and optionally verify a managed or packaged copy
of the default model against its pinned SHA-256 digest. Custom models have no
built-in expected digest.
.TP
.B model install [-y|--yes]
Download, resume, verify, and atomically install the pinned local model.
.TP
.B server [status] [--json]
Show resident llama-server status.
.TP
.B server stop [--json]
Stop only the llama-server process recorded and validated as HowTo's.
.TP
.B shell status [--json]
Show whether the Tab integration is persistently configured and active in the
current shell.
.TP
.B shell enable [--shell zsh|bash|fish]
Install or repair the embedded adapter and marked startup-file blocks. Each
existing startup file is backed up before an atomic change. Bash manages both
.I ~/.bashrc
and its active login file. A safe symlink in a startup path requires a separate,
default-No interactive approval showing its resolved target and exact managed
block; unattended invocations do not follow it. Requires completed setup.
.TP
.B shell disable [--shell zsh|bash|fish]
Remove the selected or receipt-tracked managed startup blocks, adapter, and
pending command state.
.TP
.B shell init zsh|bash|fish
Print the embedded adapter. This is primarily a diagnostic and integration
surface; normal users should use
.BR "howto setup" .
.TP
.B config [list [--json]|path|get KEY|set KEY VALUE|unset KEY]
Inspect or update HowTo's JSON configuration.
.TP
.B help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B version
Show the HowTo version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration uses schema 1 and rejects schema 0, future schemas, and unknown
keys. Stored model, llama-server, and shell paths must be absolute. The
generation limit must be smaller than the configured context size. HTTP(S)
provider URLs may include a base path but cannot include credentials, a query,
or a fragment; Unix-socket provider paths must be absolute.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOWTO_HOME
Override all HowTo data directories with one absolute path. Relative paths
are rejected. Intended for tests and portable setups.
.TP
.B HOWTO_MODEL
Use a specific GGUF model file.
.TP
.B HOWTO_PACKAGED_MODEL
Add a package-provided default-model candidate.
.TP
.B HOWTO_LLAMA_SERVER
Use a specific llama-server executable.
.TP
.B HOWTO_API_KEY
Bearer token for a configured external provider. It is removed from the
environment of a generated command approved for execution.
.TP
.B HOWTO_SHELL_SESSION
Internal non-secret per-shell identifier exported by the managed adapter. Do
not set it manually.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_CACHE_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME
Linux directory overrides. A value must be absolute when set.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Runtime-state parent on macOS or Linux. A value must be absolute when set.
.TP
.B TMPDIR
System temporary-directory override used when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is absent. A
value used for runtime state must be absolute.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/HowTo
macOS configuration, setup receipt, models, and shell adapter.
.TP
.I ~/.config/howto and ~/.local/share/howto
Linux configuration, setup receipt, models, and shell adapter.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/howto or $TMPDIR/howto-UID
Private server state and one-shot, session-scoped pending commands.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
howto setup
howto "free port 8080"
howto find files larger than 1GB
howto -x show my current IP address
howto doctor --deep
howto shell status
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
indicates success.
.TP
.B 1
indicates an operational failure or an unsuccessful diagnostic/status check.
.TP
.B 2
indicates invalid command-line usage.
.TP
.B 3
indicates a configuration, dependency, or model error.
.TP
.B 4
indicates a server, network, or model-response error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zsh (1),
.BR bash (1),
.BR fish (1)
